    {
      "title": "AISA chief Neha Bora refuses to sign peace bond, questions curbs on dissent",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/aisa-chief-neha-bora-refuses-to-sign-peace-bond-questions-curbs-on-dissent-126102400651_1.html",
      "description": "All India Students' Association president Neha Bora on Saturday said she will not sign a peace bond before a special executive magistrate, a day after the Delhi High Court dismissed her plea challenging a police notice directing her to provide a personal bond of Rs 10,000 with one surety.\nQuestioning the rationale behind the notice, Bora asked, \"Whose peace am I being asked to keep?\"\nThe police notice, issued on October 17 under Section 126 of the BNSS, asked the student leader to appear before a special executive magistrate (SEM) on October 19 and show cause as to why she should not execute a personal bond of Rs 10,000 with one surety \"for keeping peace for a period of inquiry\".\nAddressing the press at the CPI(ML) Liberation Parliamentary office here, Bora said demonstrating peacefully on the streets is a democratic right, and questioned how raising concerns against the government could be construed as a threat to peace.\n\"If we do not ask the government any questions, whose peace",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-24T09:37:03"
    }
